= Collaborative editing <features-collaborative-editing>
#set heading(outlined: false)

If configured (with server support), several people can edit the same project at once, as in Google Docs. Everyone signs in first: until you have, a card over the whole editor says "You are not signed in", with "Sign in" (also when your session ended, saying why). The others see the name you signed in with; the account is at the right of the title bar.

- You see the others' cursors with their names, and their edits as they type.
- The title bar shows the initials of everyone else in the project, the file panel who is in which file.
- Undo reverts only your own edits.

To try it in the demo, pick "Collaborate" in the playground bar and sign in with any name, then open the page in a private window and sign in as someone else.
